From 12a99a40a4d102c4ef4ec05a6ff32c02428b2e5a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 00:16:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 36/36] minicargo: accept `--flag=value` for the long options
 that take a value

Port build systems emit cargo-style `--features=lcms2,cocoa` (pngquant);
minicargo only understood `--features lcms2,cocoa` and bailed with
"Unknown flag". Split long options at the first `=` and take the value
from there, falling back to the next argv entry as before. Flags that take
no value still match the whole argument, so `--pause=1` stays an error.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 tools/minicargo/main.cpp | 94 ++++++++++++++++++++--------------------
 1 file changed, 46 insertions(+), 48 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tools/minicargo/main.cpp b/tools/minicargo/main.cpp
index aed1b894..612e24b6 100644
--- a/tools/minicargo/main.cpp
